## Error Handling Contracts

### Standard Error Response
```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "ERROR_CODE",
    "message": "Human-readable error message",
    "details": "Additional error details if applicable",
    "timestamp": "ISO 8601 timestamp",
    "requestId": "Unique request identifier"
  }
}
```

### Common Error Codes
- `AUTH_001`: Invalid JWT token
- `AUTH_002`: Expired JWT token
- `PERM_001`: Insufficient permissions
- `VALIDATION_001`: Request validation failed
- `RESOURCE_001`: Resource not found
- `SERVER_001`: Internal server error

## Performance Contracts

### Response Time SLAs
- Dashboard stats: <100ms (p95)
- Task operations: <200ms (p95)
- Preference updates: <50ms (p95)

### Animation Performance
- All animations: 60fps minimum on mid-range devices
- Entrance animations: Complete within 2 seconds
- Interactive animations: Respond within 16ms

## Security Contracts

### Authentication Requirements
- All dashboard endpoints require valid JWT token
- Token must include user_id claim
- Requests without valid token return 401 Unauthorized

### Authorization Requirements
- Users can only access their own dashboard data
- All API requests validated against user_id in JWT
- Cross-user data access prevented by backend

## Compatibility Contracts

### Browser Support
- Chrome 90+
- Firefox 88+
- Safari 14+
- Edge 90+

### Responsive Breakpoints
- Mobile: <640px
- Tablet: 640px - 1024px
- Desktop: >1024px